content.text:
`isOnline()` already existed when `3f3305e` was written, so the missing `|| !isOnline()` check was an oversight in that same commit — it's the sole introducer of the buggy condition, not the interaction of two commits.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 3f3305e469b9f5b4a21215fec35b8ef8ea0e6add

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I used `git log -p -L` on the buggy line range in `Minecraft.java` (as of the parent of the fix commit) to find when the `if (!packetHandler.isLoadingLevel){ pause(); } ...` construct was introduced. This directly located the commit that first added this conditional.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `3f3305e` replaced a simple `pause();` call (triggered by pressing Escape) with:
```java
if (!packetHandler.isLoadingLevel){
    pause();
} else {
    Mouse.setGrabbed(false);
}
```
This was meant to prevent opening the pause menu while a level is still loading (multiplayer), instead just releasing mouse grab. However, it didn't account for singleplayer/offline mode, where `packetHandler.isLoadingLevel` could be true (or otherwise not applicable) in a way that made Escape never call `pause()`, effectively breaking the pause menu in that state. The fix (`be39b28`) adds `|| !isOnline()` so that when not online (singleplayer), pressing Escape always pauses regardless of `isLoadingLevel`.

